// Browser half of omd-context-tavern.
//
// Four surfaces, one data model:
// 1. `ContextStrip` — a `conversation.input.dock` entry above the composer in
//    Bot/group sessions. It shows the epoch badge, a segmented occupancy bar
//    (system & tools / frozen prefix / active lorebook / history) with the
//    80% compaction and 95% hard-cap ticks, a hover popover that breaks the
//    used tokens down, and one wrench button that opens the Studio.
// 2. `Studio` — the full management console, portaled over the page from the
//    strip, with five tabs: 配置 (the Bot configuration hub: Bot-scoped domains
//    plus a dashed staged box for sandbox and Onlyne), 心智 (Author's Note + active mind models),
//    上下文 (engine view + rebuild prefix), 纪元 (epoch archive + history
//    escape hatch), 故事 (story notebook).
// 3. A DS-Bot details tab (上下文装配) that mounts the same Studio body
//    embedded, so the drawer is a real management surface too.
// 4. Worker chips — a message that names a worker (`onlyne://runner/issue/<id>`)
//    or the event line a Bot leaves when it hands work to the runner is
//    clickable: it opens the drawer's 电脑 tab on that worker, and the tab's
//    cards open a fullscreen spectator with one human takeover action. The
//    spectator's noVNC address is minted per open; its button asks the worker
//    to yield input control through an Onlyne `review` in the worker's thread.
//
// State lives in one JSON document per Bot project directory, owned by the
// host. This store keeps the last revision it read, sends every edit with
// that revision, and never overwrites a newer revision without the user
// explicitly choosing to reload or to overwrite.
//
// Markdown surfaces (lorebook content, author's note, story notes) render
// through marked + DOMPurify with an edit/preview toggle; media destinations
// resolve against the page's own root — the project directory on Bot pages,
// the deployment root where no session backs the page.

